  <title>4.7.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00961</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.7.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>af4f825a-0644-4454-be81-f9f8a572a816</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will work to find the slope of a line from two points, a graph, and a table. You will then use this knowledge to write equations of lines in three different forms: slope-intercept form, point-slope form, and standard form.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Write the slope of a line. </item>
  <item> Write the equation of a line in different forms. </item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 4.7.1: Evaluating Fractions </item>
  <item> 4.7.2: Finding Slope From Tables, Graphs, and Points </item>
  <list>
    <item> 4.7.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 4.7.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 4.7.3: Writing Linear Equations </item>
  <list>
    <item> 4.7.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 4.7.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 4.7.4: Writing Equations From Two Points </item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item> 4.7.5: Practice </item>
  <item> 4.7.6: Lesson Summary </item>
</list>
</section>
</content>
